# Migration Audit Log
# 
# This file tracks all data conversions and invalid data handling during migrations
# Format: CSV with headers
# 
# Fields:
# - timestamp: When the conversion occurred
# - migration_id: ID of the migration (e.g., 001_add_version_columns, 002_varchar_to_decimal)
# - table_name: Name of the table affected
# - column_name: Name of the column converted
# - record_id: ID of the affected record
# - original_value: The original value before conversion
# - converted_value: The value after conversion (usually 0 for invalid data)
# - conversion_reason: Why the conversion was performed
#
# IMPORTANT: Review this log after migration to identify records that need manual correction
# Records with invalid numeric data are converted to 0 and logged here for manual review
#
# Example entry:
# 2026-01-09T15:00:00.000Z,002_varchar_to_decimal,Products,price,123,15.99,"Invalid numeric value"
#
# Migration: 002_varchar_to_decimal
# Date: 2026-01-09
# Purpose: Convert VARCHAR to DECIMAL for numeric fields
# Action Required: Review records below and correct critical data (e.g., products with 0 price)
